{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh heard.</b> Dathan and Abiram informed against him, and he sought to kill Moses; and Moses fled, for Pharaoh was seeking to kill him — had he not hidden himself and fled from him by the power of concealment." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> They delivered him to the executioner to kill him, but the sword had no power over him. This is what Moses said (Exodus 18:4): ״ויצילני מחרב פרעה״ — 'and He delivered me from the sword of Pharaoh.'" "<b>And Moses fled from before Pharaoh.</b> From here David learned to flee, as it is said (I Samuel 19:12): ״ויברח וימלט״; (Isaiah 26:20): ״חבי כמעט רגע עד יעבר זעם״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "Source cites Exodus 18:4; the verse reads ויצילני ('He delivered me'), not ויצילנו ('He delivered us'); rendered as cited."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:40.953484109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}